meta {
  name: Load All
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/options/load
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Load Options — All Configured Underlyings

  Generates OCC option contracts for EVERY underlying in `option-tickers.txt` and
  loads their bars, replacing the in-memory store. For each underlying it pulls the
  current spot, resolves the expiry from `app.options.dte` (0 = today, 1 = tomorrow,
  ...), and generates the nearest `strikes-per-side` ITM + the same number of OTM
  strikes for each configured side (CALL/PUT). Strike spacing comes from the per-symbol
  increment in `option-tickers.txt` (e.g. `TSLA,2.5`), else `app.options.default-strike-increment`.

  Webull has no option-chain endpoint, so strikes are GENERATED. A generated strike
  that isn't actually listed returns no bars — it's logged per-contract and reported
  as `loaded:false`, but never fails the rest of the load.

  ## Response (200)
  {
    underlyings, totalContracts, totalLoaded,
    results: [ { underlying, spot, expiry, strikeIncrement, contracts, loaded,
                 occSymbols: [...], error?, loadedAt } ]
  }

  ## Notes
  - Option market data requires a paid Webull US_OPTION subscription (LIVE) or the
    sandbox environment. Without it the broker returns 401/403.
  - If a symbol's contracts all come back empty, its strike increment is probably wrong.
}
